<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/jacobrent-mark.svg">
    <title>Privacy Policy - Jacob Estate</title>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap-icons@1.11.3/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css">
    <script src="/js/theme.js"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body class="bg-soft">
    <nav class="navbar navbar-expand-lg navbar-light bg-white border-bottom sticky-top shadow-sm">
        <div class="container">
            <a class="navbar-brand brand fw-bold" href="/" aria-label="Jacob Estate home"><img class="brand-logo" src="/jacobrent-mark.svg" alt="Jacob Estate mark">Jacob Estate</a>
            <div class="d-flex gap-3 align-items-center">
                <a class="nav-link text-dark" href="/properties"><i class="bi bi-buildings me-1"></i>Browse homes</a>
                <a class="nav-link text-dark" href="/terms">Terms</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </nav>
    <main class="container legal-page py-5">
        <header class="mb-4">
            <span class="eyebrow text-uppercase">Jacob Estate</span>
            <h1 class="fw-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0">Last updated: October 27, 2026</p>
        </header>
        <article class="legal-document">
            <section>
                <h2>Information we collect</h2>
                <p>When you use Jacob Estate, we may store the name, email address, phone number, and account role you provide. Users who set up payouts provide a bank name and account number for verification. Paystack processes the full bank details; Jacob Estate stores Paystack recipient or subaccount codes, account holder name, bank name, and last four account digits, not the full account number. We store property listings, ratings, comments, rental booking messages, sale inquiries and statuses, and payment references needed to operate the service. Property owners upload a video tour for each listing; videos are stored with our video hosting provider, Cloudinary, and only the video link and identifier are kept in our database. If you sign in with Google, we receive your verified email address and name from Google.</p>
            </section>
            <section>
                <h2>How information is used</h2>
                <p>We use this information to create and secure accounts, display listings, connect home seekers and property owners, manage rental bookings and sale inquiries, verify rental payment status, and maintain the service. Account and listing information may be visible to other users where needed for those features.</p>
            </section>
            <section>
                <h2>Payments, cookies, and storage</h2>
                <p>Rental payments are completed through Paystack's hosted checkout. Jacob Estate does not store payment card details. Paystack processes and stores property-owner payout account details for split settlement. The app stores rental payment references, amounts, outcomes, and masked payout details to keep booking and payout records accurate. Sale inquiries are not purchase payments.</p>
                <p>The app uses a session cookie to keep you signed in and local browser storage to remember your display-theme preference. Data is stored by the service's configured database and hosting providers.</p>
            </section>
            <section>
                <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
                <p>We share information with the relevant home seeker or property owner when needed to provide listing, rental booking, and sale inquiry features, and with service providers that support hosting, database storage, payment processing, or transactional email delivery (including password-reset and seller-inquiry notifications). We do not use the app to collect card details. Administrator actions on listings, accounts and payouts are recorded in an audit log that includes the administrator's email address and IP address, to protect users and detect misuse.</p>
                <p>We retain account, listing, and booking information for as long as needed to operate the service, meet operational requirements, and maintain transaction records. Accounts with payment records cannot be deleted while those records must be kept for accounting and dispute purposes. Do not include sensitive personal information in listing descriptions or booking messages.</p>
            </section>
            <section>
                <h2>Your choices and questions</h2>
                <p>You can review or update available account details from your profile page. For privacy questions or requests concerning your information, contact the Jacob Estate administrator through the official channel provided by the service operator.</p>
            </section>
        </article>
    </main>
    <%- include('partials/legal-footer') %>
</body>
</html>